        "original_id": "06e0916d-f4e8-5bcf-84a8-a9e6bd9f616b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Oscar W. Koch, George S. Patton Jr.\n- Roles: brigadier general, intelligence officer (G-2), army commander\n- Organizations: U.S. Army, U.S. Third Army, U.S. Seventh Army\n- Events: World War II, Allied invasion of Normandy\n\nFacts:\n- George S. Patton Jr. was born on November 11, 1885, and died on December 21, 1945.\n- Oscar W. Koch was born on January 10, 1897, in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, and died on May 16, 1970, in Carbondale, Illinois.\n- During World War II, George S. Patton Jr. was a senior officer of the United States Army.\n- During World War II, George S. Patton Jr. commanded the U.S. Seventh Army in the Mediterranean and European theaters.\n- Following the Allied invasion of Normandy in June 1944, George S. Patton Jr. became best known for leading the U.S. Third Army in France and Germany.\n- During World War II, Oscar W. Koch was a brigadier general in the U.S. Army.\n- During World War II, Oscar W. Koch served as the Third Army intelligence officer, designated G-2, while George S. Patton Jr. commanded the army.",
